1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
[Kurapika]
This country's open to tourists.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,000
That's where Killua is?

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,000
It'll take three days to reach by airship.

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,000
When do you think we should leave?

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
-Today! Right now!
-Alright! I'm with Gon.

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Got it. I'll order the tickets then.

7
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,000
[theme music playing]

8
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:51,000
[Killua]
I'm from a family of assassins, so yeah,

9
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:52,000
they're all in the business of murder.

10
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:58,000
And my entire family,
they've got real high hopes for me.

11
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,000
But y'know, I can't stand it.

12
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Who wants their whole life mapped out
for them?

13
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Killua...

14
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,000
So, what's the deal
with the long face, Gon?

15
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,000
By tomorrow, we'll be in Padokea.

16
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:19,000
You'll see Killua soon.

17
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Yup!

18
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,000
[Gon] We'll definitely bring Killua
back with us!

19
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:33,000
A x DANGEROUS x WATCHDOG

20
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,000
[narrator] Gon, Leorio, and Kurapika
have arrived in the Dentora region

21
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:46,000
of the Republic of Padokea,
which Killua calls home.

22
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:58,000
[Leorio] I can almost see it.
So that's where the assassins' base is?

23
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:02,000
-It looks kind of creepy, doesn't it?
-[Kurapika] It does.

24
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Once we arrive,
we should gather information.

25
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,000
[Leorio] Okay.

26
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
[Shopkeeper] Kukuroo Mountain...

27
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:13,000
You'll want to take
the scenic mountain bus tour over there.

28
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:17,000
It only runs once a day, but you'll have
a guide to show you around.

29
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:24,000
[tour guide] I'd like to thank all of you
for choosing Lamentation Tours.

30
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,000
It's an honor to have you here.

31
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Now, get ready, because we'll be making
our way up to Kukuroo Mountain,

32
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:35,000
home to the Zoldyck family of assassins.

33
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:37,000
Check it out.

34
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
No way those guys are tourists.

35
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,000
-True.
-[tour guide] Okay, everyone!

36
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,000
If you'll all look out the window
to your right...

37
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,000
[Gon gasps]

38
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:54,000
...you'll see Kukuroo Mountain
where the Zoldyck family lives.

39
00:03:55,000 --> 00:04:00,000
It's 3,722-meter high,
and it's surrounded by forest.

40
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:04,000
The Zoldyck estate is rumored to be
somewhere on the mountain.

41
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,000
although no one has ever actually seen it.

42
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:10,000
The Zoldyck family consists
of ten members:

43
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Mother and Father, five siblings,
grandparents and great-grandfather,

44
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:19,000
all of whom are assassins!

45
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:24,000
Alright, now hold on, while we get
a little closer to the mountain.

46
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,000
Would you look at that...

47
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:36,000
This is the front gate
of the Zoldyck estate.

48
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:39,000
No one who's entered
has ever returned alive,

49
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:43,000
which has earned this gate the nickname
"the Door to Hades."

50
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:48,000
To enter, you have to go through the door
by the security checkpoint.

51
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:52,000
But beyond that is private property,
so this is as far as we can go.

52
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:56,000
[Leorio] Hold on! This is the front gate?
The mountain is all the way over there!

53
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:02,000
That's right. The Zoldyck family
own Kukuroo Mountain, every inch of it,

54
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:05,000
not to mention all the surrounding land.

55
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:08,000
So, what you're telling me
is this is their front yard?

56
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:10,000
-Miss Tour Guide?
-Yes?

57
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:14,000
What are we gonna have to do
to get inside?

58
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Hmm. Oh, dear.
You were paying attention, right?

59
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,000
Yeah, but you didn't say--

60
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:23,000
If you go inside,
you'll never come out again!

61
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,000
It's an assassins' hideout.

62
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,000
-It's a sham.
-Huh?

63
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:31,000
A family of assassins
no one's ever seen?

64
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,000
If we can just snap a picture of them,

65
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,000
we're gonna get a hundred million
in reward money.

66
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:41,000
Are you kidding me? Damn it!
I should have taken a picture of Killua!

67
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,000
[both groan]

68
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,000
They probably rely on the mystique
to protect them.

69
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:49,000
I bet the truth is a whole lot
less interesting.

70
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:53,000
Huh?

71
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:54,000
[yells]

72
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:58,000
-Open up the gate!
-I'm afraid I can't.

73
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:01,000
The master of the house would not approve
of such a thing.

74
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:03,000
Don't worry about that.

75
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:06,000
We kinda figured
we'd kill your master anyway.

76
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:10,000
[sighs]

77
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:15,000
[guard grunts]

78
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:18,000
-[moans]
-Are you okay?

79
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:23,000
-Yes, I'll be alright.
-[gate creaking open]

80
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:28,000
Oh, darn! The master hates it
when Mike snacks between meals.

81
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:32,000
-What?
-[men yelling]

82
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:45,000
[all gasp]

83
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:47,000
[all yelp]

84
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,000
[screams]

85
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:55,000
[everyone clamoring]

86
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,000
[guard] Well, damn it.

87
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:04,000
Mike's only supposed to eat
at designated times.

88
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Mike!

89
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:08,000
Don't blame those extra pounds on me!

90
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:10,000
What was that thing?

91
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:23,000
Hey, you guys! What are you doing?
Time to get back on the bus!

92
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:28,000
Go ahead without us
'cause we're all staying here.

93
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:29,000
What?

94
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,000
[guard] I see.

95
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:44,000
So, you're young Master Killua's friends,
are you?

96
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,000
Happy to hear it.

97
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:51,000
I've worked here for the past 20 years,
and to the best of my recollection,

98
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:54,000
you three are the first friends
who've ever come to visit.

99
00:07:57,000 --> 00:08:01,000
Now, I probably shouldn't be telling you
this, seeing as how I work here,

100
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:05,000
but this place is pretty lonely.
No one ever really visits.

101
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:10,000
Well, except those types.
We get our fair share of those. [chuckles]

102
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:15,000
But a family of assassins
is bound to be unusual.

103
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:17,000
I guess that's the price
they have to pay.

104
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:21,000
Oh, well. Anyways,
I'm so glad you're here.

105
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,000
-Thank you for coming.
-Don't mention it.

106
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,000
However...

107
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:29,000
That doesn't mean I'm going to be able
to let any of you inside.

108
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:35,000
You saw it earlier, didn't you?
How huge the beast's arm was?

109
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:41,000
That arm belongs to Mike.
It's the Zoldycks' watchdog.

110
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:44,000
It only obeys the family
and attacks everyone else.

111
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:50,000
As a matter of fact, it's still following
the order its master gave ten years ago...

112
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:56,000
To kill every single intruder
who tries to get inside.

113
00:08:56,000 --> 00:09:01,000
I guess he isn't following it technically
because he keeps eating them.

114
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,000
[laughs]

115
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:06,000
But, like I was saying,
I can't let you in.

116
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:08,000
I wouldn't want friends
of young Master Killua

117
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:13,000
being stripped down to their skeletons.
[laughs]

118
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:16,000
Question. How is it that you're safe here?

119
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:20,000
-Hmm?
-It's just, you can go inside.

120
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:22,000
and if you were never allowed to go in,

121
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:25,000
it's unlikely
that you would be given a key.

122
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:28,000
Hmm, that's very perceptive,

123
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:31,000
but the fact is,
you're only about half right.

124
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:35,000
See, I don't need a key to get inside.

125
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:39,000
This key was specially made
for intruders only.

126
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:41,000
There's a key for intruders?

127
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,000
Almost all of them
go right for the front gate.

128
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:48,000
About 90 percent.
I couldn't begin to tell you why, though.

129
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:52,000
If I don't open the gate for them,

130
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:56,000
every time without fail,
they try to break it down.

131
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:58,000
They're real troublemakers, these types.

132
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:02,000
That's why we added a locked door
to one side. It works pretty well.

133
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:07,000
They just take the key from the poor,
helpless security guard,

134
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,000
and then Mike eats them.
It's as simple as that.

135
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:12,000
[Kurapika] A locked door?

136
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,000
That's it!

137
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:19,000
As you just realized,
I'm not a security guard.

138
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:22,000
I'm just the janitor
who cleans up after Mike,

139
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:25,000
So, the front gate isn't actually locked
after all.

140
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:27,000
-Exactly.
-What?

141
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:35,000
HUNTER GLOSSARY

142
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:39,000
LAMENTATION TOUR

143
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:07,000
I've pushed and pulled
but it won't budge!

144
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,000
Are you sure the gate isn't locked?

145
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:11,000
[guard]
I'm afraid you're just not strong enough.

146
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:14,000
Shut up! I was giving it
everything I've got!

147
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,000
Step back and watch.

148
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:27,000
This gate is officially known
as the Testing Gate,

149
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:30,000
because anyone who's not strong enough
to open it...

150
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,000
-[grunts]
-[gust of wind blows]

151
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:36,000
...is considered unworthy of entering
the Zoldyck estate.

152
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:43,000
[grunts]

153
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:45,000
[all gasp]

154
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:52,000
[door thuds shut]

155
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:55,000
So, you can see that the door
closes automatically,

156
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:58,000
so you'll want to slip inside
as soon as it opens.

157
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:01,000
And you won't need to worry about Mike.

158
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:05,000
He has strict orders not to attack anyone
who enters through the Testing Gate.

159
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:10,000
Whew. The older I get,
the tougher this seems to become.

160
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,000
But they'll fire me
if I can't open the gate,

161
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,000
so, I need to stay fit.

162
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:19,000
And I should mention,
the first doors weigh two tons each.

163
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:23,000
What? You're really not supposed
to be able to...

164
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:25,000
Wait, what did you say?

165
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:29,000
-Did you say the first doors?
-Yeah, take a look.

166
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:32,000
There are seven doors in all.

167
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:37,000
And keep in mind that each set is twice
as heavy as the set of doors before it.

168
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:38,000
[Leorio] Twice?

169
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:42,000
The more force you put into it,
the more doors you open.

170
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,000
Gotta be pretty strong
to get through all of them.

171
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:49,000
Incidentally, when young Master Killua
returned to the estate,

172
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:52,000
he opened three of them, just like that.

173
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:56,000
Three? That's like...12 tons!

174
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:59,000
-It's 16 tons, Gon.
-[laughs]

175
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,000
[guard] Starting to get it now?

176
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:04,000
This is what it takes
just to get through the door.

177
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:07,000
They live in a completely different world.

178
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:11,000
[Gon] I don't like that.
May I borrow the key?

179
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:17,000
I didn't come all this way to be tested.
I came so I could see my friend.

180
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:19,000
Think of me as an intruder.

181
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:22,000
So please, let me borrow the key.

182
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:24,000
and I'll go in there
through the intruder's door.

183
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:26,000
-Gon!
-Hey.

184
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:29,000
Lend it to me, or don't,
but I'm getting in.

185
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:31,000
I'll climb the wall if I have to.

186
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:35,000
[Leorio] Don't be stupid, Gon!
Didn't you see that terrifying monster?

187
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:39,000
Its forearm was bigger than
your whole body times two!

188
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:40,000
I told you, I don't like this!

189
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:44,000
Why test your friends? It's crazy!

190
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:47,000
There's no way
I'm ever going through that door.

191
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:52,000
You're right, but if you think
you can force your way in, think again.

192
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:56,000
It's absolutely impossible.
Mike will definitely kill you.

193
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:58,000
I have to agree with you.

194
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:01,000
We have the time,
so let's find a way to use the first door.

195
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:08,000
No use.

196
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:10,000
He won't change his mind
when he's like this.

197
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:11,000
Yes, you're right.

198
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:16,000
[sighs] I'm sorry to say this,
but I can't let you have the key.

199
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:20,000
I won't feed young Master Killua's friends
to Mike. I can't do it.

200
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:21,000
Guess I don't have it in me.

201
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:24,000
But would you wait here
for a minute, please?

202
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:30,000
[dial tone]

203
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:33,000
[guard] Hello, this is Zebro.

204
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:38,000
Sorry to call. It's just that three
of young Master Killua's friends are here

205
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:40,000
and they would very much like to see him.

206
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:44,000
Yes. Yes, I'm sorry. Of course.

207
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:49,000
Yes, I understand. Yes. Yes.
I'm so very sorry to disturb you.

208
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:55,000
-Yeah, I figured I would get yelled at.
-You called up to the house for us?

209
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:59,000
No, I was speaking
with the Zoldyck family's butler.

210
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:03,000
All communication with the mansion
has to go through the butler first.

211
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:06,000
It's not easy
to reach the family members directly.

212
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:11,000
Could you get him on the phone again?
I'd like to talk to him this time.

213
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:16,000
Well, I suppose I can, but I guarantee
that you're not going to enjoy it.

214
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:18,000
[pressing buttons]

215
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:22,000
[butler]
You've reached the butler's quarters.

216
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:26,000
My name is Gon, and I'm one
of Killua's friends that came to visit.

217
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:28,000
Is Killua there? Can I speak to him?

218
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:33,000
Master Killua does not have friends.

219
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:35,000
[puts down phone]

220
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:46,000
[dial tone]

221
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:48,000
[butler]
You've reached the butler's quarters.

222
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:54,000
How could you possibly know that, huh?
Put Killua on the phone!

223
00:15:56,000 --> 00:16:00,000
-I believe you said your name is Gon?
-[Gon] Yeah.

224
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:04,000
[butler] Let us pretend that Master Killua
does have a friend named Gon.

225
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,000
There is no proof that you are him.

226
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,000
Put him on the phone, he'll recognize me!

227
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:12,000
[butler] By your voice?
That is no guarantee.

228
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,000
[Gon] Put him on the phone,
he'll recognize me!

229
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:18,000
[butler] That was a simple recording.

230
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:22,000
but there are many other ways
to mimic someone's voice.

231
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Next, you'll say
that he'd recognize you by sight.

232
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:29,000
There aren't as many methods

233
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:32,000
by which you could perfectly replicate
someone's appearance,

234
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:34,000
but it isn't impossible.

235
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:38,000
Or perhaps you are Gon,
but someone has coerced you

236
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:42,000
to approach Master Killua
for some sinister motive.

237
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:46,000
As long as that threat exists,
I cannot let you meet with him.

238
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:54,000
The Zoldyck family
are in the assassination business.

239
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,000
They have their enemies, of course.

240
00:16:56,000 --> 00:17:01,000
And it is a butler's responsibility
to guard them from those enemies.

241
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:04,000
Apologies, you will have to leave.

242
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Hey! Wait!

243
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:12,000
Gon!

244
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:18,000
He's really pissed, isn't he?

245
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:20,000
I think he's going to climb over the wall.

246
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:21,000
He what?

247
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:26,000
[Leorio] Hey, Gon! Knock it off!

248
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:29,000
It's okay. You two can wait here.

249
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:31,000
-I'm going in alone.
-I can't let you do that!

250
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:34,000
-[Gon] I'll be fine!
-[Leorio] No, you won't!

251
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:36,000
[Kurapika]
Look, both of you need to calm down!

252
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:39,000
[Leorio] I'm perfectly calm!
Now, come on, get down!

253
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:41,000
[Kurapika] He's right. Don't be stupid.

254
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:46,000
Here, Gon, I'll give you the key.
You can go through the door, alright?

255
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:50,000
Just wait a second, Pops!
We can convince him to stop this.

256
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:53,000
Oh, really? Because he strikes me
as the stubborn type.

257
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:58,000
To make amends, I've decided
to accompany you through the door.

258
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:00,000
What?

259
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:04,000
Mike knows me well enough
to recognize me.

260
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:07,000
and it's possible he might not attack
if he sees I'm with you.

261
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:11,000
Though I'm almost 100 percent certain
that he'll just kill us all.

262
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:16,000
I can't let you do that.
I don't want to cause any trouble for you.

263
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:20,000
Too late. I'm coming.
There'd be trouble even if I stayed.

264
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:24,000
If I send young Master Killua's friends
to their deaths,

265
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:27,000
I'd never be able
to look him in the eye again.

266
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:31,000
If you die, well,
then I'll die alongside you.

267
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:39,000
I understand, sir.

268
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:42,000
I guess I didn't stop
to think about your situation.

269
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:43,000
Sorry.

270
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:49,000
[guard] He's a good kid.

271
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:53,000
ready and willing to put aside
his own anger for the sake of another.

272
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:56,000
He believes in his own strength.

273
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:59,000
and he believes in his friends
just as much.

274
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:02,000
He has such a strong heart.

275
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:06,000
In fact, it's likely that
Mike won't frighten him at all.

276
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:08,000
You like animals, don't you, Gon?

277
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:10,000
Huh? Yes.

278
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:12,000
I thought you might.

279
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:15,000
And did you grow up
playing in the countryside?

280
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:18,000
Yes! How did you know all that?

281
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:22,000
Alright, in just a moment, I'm going
to open the Testing Gate again.

282
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:25,000
I want you to see Mike with your own eyes.

283
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:39,000
Hey, are you sure that it's okay
for us to come in?

284
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:42,000
Of course. You entered through
the Testing Gate, so you'll be fine.

285
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:46,000
Mike! Come here!

286
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:54,000
[Mike growling in distance]

287
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:13,000
[Gon gasps]

288
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:31,000
[guard] So, Gon, do you understand?

289
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:35,000
This is a hunting beast,
and a highly trained one at that!

290
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:39,000
It's like no animal
you've ever encountered in the wild

291
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:41,000
No, not by a long shot.

292
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:44,000
You believed you could
communicate with him

293
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:47,000
until you looked in his eyes, right?

294
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:50,000
As we speak,

295
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Mike is memorizing the appearances
and scents of these new humans.

296
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:57,000
There isn't anything else on his mind
at the moment.

297
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:59,000
He's just like a machine.

298
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:04,000
So, Gon, do you think you could fight him?

299
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:08,000
I'd be too scared.
I don't ever want to fight him!

300
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:13,000
[guard chuckles]
He's an honest lad, too.

301
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:17,000
Well, how long will you be staying here?

302
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:19,000
Until we see Killua!

303
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:22,000
We're not leaving a second before!

304
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:25,000
[chuckles]

305
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:27,000
Alright then, follow me.

306
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:36,000
[narrator]
First, The Testing Gate, and now Mike.

307
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:39,000
Between the two of them,
Gon has seen for himself

308
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:43,000
that the Zoldyck family truly live
in a completely different world.

309
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:48,000
However, Gon had made a promise
to himself

310
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:51,000
that no matter what difficulties lay
on the path ahead of him

311
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:54,000
in the end, he would see Killua.

312
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:00,000
[theme music plays]

313
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:24,000
[Gon] Next time, "The Guard's Duty."
Five times five is 25.

314
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:26,000
[Kurapika] So, you know how to do math?

315
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:29,000
[Kurapika, Gon and Leorio]
Five times five is 25!
